== TASK: additively ADD the whole-message SEND family + subscribe + xpub_recv ==
This phase is ADDITIVE — keep every existing *_part function working (removal is a later phase). Add:

Public decls in core/include/zlink/socket/api.h (signatures verbatim from draft §7.4):
  zlink_send(s, zlink_msg_t* parts, size_t part_count, flags, user_context, completion_id_out)
  zlink_send_rid(s, target_rid, parts, part_count, flags, user_context, completion_id_out)
  zlink_request(s, target_router_rid_or_null, parts, part_count, flags, timeout_ms, user_context, completion_id_out)
  zlink_reply(s, source_rid, reply_token, parts, part_count)
  zlink_publish(subject, topic_id, parts, part_count, flags)
  zlink_subscribe(sub, source_rid_out, topic_id_buf, topic_id_capacity, topic_id_len_out,
                  parts_out, parts_capacity, part_count_out, flags)   // recv, replaces subscribe_part
  zlink_xpub_recv(...)   // SAME signature/contract as zlink_xpub_recv_part, new name (no zlink_msg_t)

Implement each next to its part-based sibling (keep the sibling):
  - socket_message_send_api.cpp: zlink_send / zlink_send_rid / zlink_publish (siblings at :590/:677/:775)
  - socket_request_reply_submit_api.cpp: zlink_request / zlink_reply (siblings at :1098/:1190).
    NOTE: zlink_request_part had "MORE => timeout_ms==0 && user_context==NULL" constraints; whole-record
    zlink_request submits the whole record at once so those per-part constraints do not apply.
  - socket_message_api.cpp: zlink_subscribe (recv; sibling zlink_subscribe_part at :463) — topic buffer
    idiom identical, parts filled like zlink_recv (array+capacity+count, adopt into caller slots).
  - xpub: add zlink_xpub_recv delegating to the same impl as zlink_xpub_recv_part (both names live).

Implementation approach (send): iterate the caller parts array once inside Core, submitting each part
with the existing internal per-part submit path applying MORE for i<count-1 and FINAL for i==count-1,
as ONE atomic record (same staging/atomicity the *_part loop produced, but caller makes one call).
Contracts to honor:
  - Every slot's msg is consumed by the call (like "Every call consumes part_"). D63-8: whole-record
    retry only — on failure the record is not partially submitted (all-or-nothing per the result code;
    mirror the existing failed-FINAL-discards-staged-prefix behavior but at the record level).
  - record atomicity, thread-safety/single-consumer unchanged. No numbers fabrication.
  - part_count==0 -> EINVAL. NULL required args -> EFAULT.
- libzlink.vers: ADD the new symbols (keep the old ones this phase).
